      "writtenOn": "2024-05-10T14:04:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we set this to `nullptr`, if we ever call `dawnRenderPipeline()` a second time, we\u0027d try waiting on the future again. \n\nWhen the callback is finished, regardless of success or not, should we set the future to null? Then if it holds both a null wgpu::RenderPipeline and a null future, it\u0027s in a failure state and we don\u0027t try waiting anymore. If it was a successful compilation, we\u0027ve freed some memory held by the future.",
