      "writtenOn": "2024-05-10T14:04:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in theory, the compilation could fail if we have a bug in our sksl or sksl-\u003ewgsl, or if there\u0027s a driver compiler bug, right? For sksl or sksl-\u003ewgsl, or wgsl-\u003ebackend shader, an assert here seems like an okay signal that something is wrong since those are bugs that we can control.\n\nBut if it\u0027s a driver compiler bug that causes the pipeline to fail, we need to clean up gracefully and we\u0027d want to mark the whole `DawnGraphicsPipeline` as bad and fail the `insertRecording`. Ideally we\u0027d also then remove this `DawnGraphicsPipeline` from the global pipeline cache since it\u0027ll never recover, but if we keep it in the cache, then future recordings will keep using that pipeline and hit the null `wgpu::RenderPipeline`.\n\nIn that case, I think we need some way to mark the `DawnGraphicsPipeline` as bad and then fail the `insertRecording`.",
      "range": {
